WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Compliance Evidence Pack: audit-grade records from your agents — generated, mapped and accepted, not improvised the week before the audit.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:15.000
The problem: Colorado wants three years of records and 30-day explanations from January 2027; ISO 42001 certificates have more than tripled in four months; and SOC 2 has no AI-specific controls, so auditors are improvising.

3
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:29.000
What it does: a tamper-evident, hash-chained recorder; versions and approvals attached to every decision; scheduled evaluations; four exports; mapping to ISO 42001, CSA, NIST, the EU AI Act and OWASP; and a push into Vanta or Drata.

4
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:41.000
The deliverable: one decision followed from intent to export — the chained steps, the versions, the human reviewer, the 30-day explanation and the frameworks it maps to. The figures shown are a sample.

5
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:50.000
How it ships: built February to April 2027 on the Governor's event log; design partners get the recorder at cost; first real audits mid-2027; gate five on 30 June 2027 — an auditor has accepted it, or we say so.

6
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Published licence prices: design partners $6,000 a year, locked for two years, with an auditor in the room; general availability $12,000 to $30,000 a year per estate.

7
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:05.000
Design partners wanted for the second quarter of 2027 — rainkernel.com or hello@rainkernel.com.
